Disables Jekyll on GitHub Pages.

Without this file Pages runs the published tree through Jekyll, which EXCLUDES
every directory whose name begins with an underscore. This world keeps its
private modules exactly that way — scenes/_plans/ (the five coordinate spaces),
scenes/_close/ (95 generated close-ups), assets/*/_kit.mjs and the rest — so
Jekyll was 404ing the five plan modules the periodic table imports when you
click a PLACE, and would have 404'd anything else under an underscore later.

It failed as a 404 inside a dynamic import, which surfaces as a plan that
simply never draws: no error on the page, nothing in the console the user would
look at. Found by checking every URL the atlas loads rather than by opening the
page and glancing at it.
